     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pattern and exception",
     "texto": [
      "In many stressed words, a short vowel is followed by a double consonant or a consonant cluster, while a long vowel usually precedes a single consonant. It's a useful pattern, not a rule without exceptions. The actual length and other features depend on the word and variety; check against reliable audio."
